        "canonical_name_en": "Enheduanna",
        "disposition": "move_to_culture",
        "basis": "Although Enheduanna held the high-priestly office of Nanna, modern Assyriological and literary-history authorities identify her above all as the first known named author in world literature. Under v2, that durable literary identity fits culture more directly than office-based religion.",
        "sources": [
          "https://yalebooks.yale.edu/book/9780300276763/enheduana/",
          "https://newsarchive.berkeley.edu/news/media/releases/2001/03/06_poems.html"
        ]
      },
      {
        "canonical_name_en": "Lalla Fatma N'Soumer",
        "disposition": "move_to_military",
        "basis": "Her spiritual authority is historically relevant, but her ATLAS Activity and historical scholarship center on leading armed Kabyle resistance against the French conquest. Warfare and armed leadership therefore fit military more directly than religion.",
        "sources": [
          "https://asjp.cerist.dz/en/downArticle/364/2/1/130841",
          "https://asjp.cerist.dz/en/article/247924"
        ]
      },
      {
        "canonical_name_en": "Martin Luther King Jr.",
        "disposition": "move_to_culture",
        "basis": "King was a Baptist pastor and drew deeply on Christian theology, but his durable representative historical identity is leadership of the U.S. civil-rights movement and nonviolent social thought. Because v2 assigns social thought to culture and he did not exercise religious institutional leadership as his primary historical role, culture is the direct fit.",
        "sources": [
          "https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/peace/1964/king/biographical/",
          "https://kinginstitute.stanford.edu/mia-forms-elects-king-president"
        ]
      },
      {
        "canonical_name_en": "Ali ibn Abi Talib",
        "disposition": "retain_religion",
        "basis": "Ali also ruled as fourth caliph, but his enduring identity as a foundational Islamic figure and, in Shi'i tradition, the first Imam makes religion at least as structurally central as the political office. The single-domain rule therefore retains religion rather than mechanically mapping a caliphal reign to governance.",
        "sources": [
          "https://www.iranicaonline.org/articles/ali-b-abi-taleb/"
        ]
      },
      {
        "canonical_name_en": "Ngawang Lobsang Gyatso",
        "disposition": "retain_religion",
        "basis": "The Fifth Dalai Lama was explicitly both spiritual and political leader of Tibet. His representative identity remains the Dalai Lama institution, so the political role does not override the religious identity under the no-Role-to-Domain rule.",
        "sources": [
          "https://tibet.net/about-tibet/his-holiness/"
        ]
      },
      {
        "canonical_name_en": "Te Kooti Arikirangi Te Turuki",
        "disposition": "retain_religion",
        "basis": "Te Kooti was simultaneously a guerrilla leader, prophet and founder of the Ringatu faith. Because he created a durable faith tradition that survived the war phase, religion remains the better single representative domain.",
        "sources": [
          "https://teara.govt.nz/en/biographies/1t45/te-kooti-arikirangi-te-turuki",
          "https://nzhistory.govt.nz/people/te-kooti-arikirangi-te-turuki"
        ]
      },
      {
